---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-10-17';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclosure"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Disclosure', path: '/disclosure/' },
  ]}
  description="How singletenant.ai handles referral links, advertising, and sponsorship, which relationships exist, and why none of them affects the data."
>
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="m-0 mb-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Disclosure
      </h1>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs mb-10" style="color: var(--color-mute);">
        Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This site is independent. It may earn money from referral links,
          advertising, and sponsorship. This page lists every commercial
          relationship and sets out the rules that keep them apart from the
          data.
        </p>

        <h2 id="independence">What money never affects</h2>
        <p>
          Advertising, sponsorship, and referral commission never influence:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>the vendor matrix, or any fact recorded in it;</li>
          <li>the ordering of vendors, which is alphabetical;</li>
          <li>the comparison pages, which are generated from the same data;</li>
          <li>
            which vendors are included, which follows the published
            <a href="/methodology/">inclusion criteria</a> only.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Vendor facts are verified against primary sources, and every
          populated fact links to its evidence with the date it was checked. A
          fact that cannot be verified is shown as "Not verified" whatever the
          vendor's commercial relationship with this site. Advertisers and
          sponsors get no preview of, or say over, editorial content. The
          <a href="/editorial-policy/#conflicts">editorial policy</a> covers
          conflicts of interest in full.
        </p>

        <h2 id="referral-links">Referral links</h2>
        <p>
          Some outbound links are referral links. If you follow one and become
          a customer of that vendor, this site may earn a commission. You pay
          nothing extra. Every referral link is marked where it appears: a
          visible "Referral link" notice sits next to it, and the link carries
          the <code>rel="sponsored"</code> attribute. A link without that
          notice is not a referral link.
        </p>

        <h2 id="advertising">Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          If the site carries advertising, each ad sits in a clearly marked
          slot labelled "Advertisement", separate from the editorial content.
          Ads never appear inside the vendor matrix, a comparison table, or a
          vendor's facts, and buying an ad buys nothing else.
        </p>

        <h2 id="sponsorship">Sponsored content</h2>
        <p>
          Sponsored content is always labelled "Sponsored" at the top, with the
          sponsor named, and links to this page. Sponsors do not write or
          approve the vendor data, and sponsored content is never presented as
          independent analysis. Sponsored links carry
          <code>rel="sponsored"</code>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="relationships">Current relationships</h2>
        <p>
          This site has an affiliate relationship with <strong>RunPod</strong>.
          It has no advertisers or sponsors, and no other vendor in the
          database has a commercial relationship with this site. This list is
          updated whenever a relationship starts or ends, and the change is
          recorded in the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
        <p>
          Identifying paid-for content and links is required by the UK CAP
          Code (enforced by the ASA) and, for US readers, the FTC's endorsement
          guides (16 CFR Part 255). Questions about this policy:
          <a href="mailto:simon@singletenant.ai">simon@singletenant.ai</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
